                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fc8994e-a9b7-4e27-b6a0-d9f2ac5964dd",
                                                "sense_id": "78123630-a495-37c9-93bc-e9f0d6f58cca",
                                                "text": "Holonyms: Stone Age < prehistory"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b54759b4-1a46-4b62-89c3-83cd19372033",
                                                "sense_id": "78123630-a495-37c9-93bc-e9f0d6f58cca",
                                                "text": "Meronyms: Pre-Pottery Neolithic, Pre-Pottery Neolithic A, Pre-Pottery Neolithic B"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Neolithic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "506f9890-f7f2-3e0b-8f7d-f87bd3a99e09",
                                        "entry_id": "89b7dad1-fa5c-3133-b6fa-b0429be7fab9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to the New Stone Age."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a76275c7-dd24-4507-9e66-be120fc0eade",
                                                "sense_id": "506f9890-f7f2-3e0b-8f7d-f87bd3a99e09",
                                                "text": "Tokens are first identified at around the same time as the local peoples changed from a life based on hunting and gathering to one based on agriculture. The tokens, as Schmandt-Besserat says, \"were part and parcel of the Neolithic phenomenon; that is, the so-called agricultural revolution.\" (Before Writing 41)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c256d5a-9d38-40ed-870f-79461026426d",
                                                "sense_id": "506f9890-f7f2-3e0b-8f7d-f87bd3a99e09",
                                                "text": "... I was fascinated by a pair of stories about a Neolithic girl who wrote the first letter, and invented the first alphabet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Neolithic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "795fe14c-09b0-38dd-a1ab-759823be052e",
                                        "entry_id": "9cecb260-8003-31ab-8112-1f129c462dec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who lived during the New Stone Age."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5040be65-028b-4b86-8d0f-f0d570b4978c",
                                                "sense_id": "795fe14c-09b0-38dd-a1ab-759823be052e",
                                                "text": "For the Neolithics, the stone was flint, and it's still impressive to see what they were able to achieve with it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "33bc8ca6-c3a2-4d02-8090-298e6d6f7e20",
                        "source_entry_id": "d4bfb6bd-5ba2-38c5-a4dc-f82be0e0fdc7",
